   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to requiring the state comptroller to conduct audits of private water utility companies prior to and after rate changes are approved by the public service commission",
    "basePrintNo": "S6862",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6862-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §89-c, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6862\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to requiring the\nstate comptroller to conduct audits of private water utility companies\nprior to and after rate changes are approved by the public service\ncommission\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation would require the state comptroller to conduct audits\nof private water utility companies prior to and after rate changes are\napproved by the public service commission.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSubdivision 10 of section 89-c of the public service law is amended\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nNearly ninety-five percent of all New Yorkers receive water from\npublic water supply systems in New York State. Private water utility\ncompanies service the remaining customers.\n\nConsumers have no choice who provides their water. Public water\nutilities are exempt from property taxes. Private water utilities are\nnot. Private water utilities can pass the expense of these taxes on to\ntheir customers and create bills, which in many cases, are\ndramatically higher than public water utilities.\n\nWhen private companies seek and receive rate increases from the Public\nService Commission, the corresponding water bill spikes can be\ndramatic. Consumers required to pay these large charges deserve to\nknow that the company's finances are in order and that all laws\nregulating their costs, profits and expenditures are being followed.\n\nThis legislation would require the state comptroller to conduct audits\nof private water utility companies prior to and one year after rate\nchanges are approved by the public service commission.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
