    "lawCode": "Amd §89-c, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6862A\n\nSPONSOR: MARCELLINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to requiring the\npublic service commission retain an independent auditor to conduct\naudits of private water utility companies prior to and after rate chang-\nes are approved by the public service commission\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would require the public service commission to retain\nan independent auditor to conduct audits of private water utility compa-\nnies prior to and after rate changes are approved by the public service\ncommission.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSubdivision 10 of section 89-c of the public service law is amended to\nrequire the public service commission to retain an independent auditor\nto conduct audits of private water utility companies prior to and after\nrate changes are approved by the public service commission.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNearly ninety-five percent of all New Yorkers receive water from public\nwater supply systems in New York State. Private water utility companies\nservice the remaining customers.\n\nConsumers have no choice who provides their water. Public water utili-\nties are exempt from property taxes. Private water utilities are not.\nPrivate water utilities can pass the expense of these taxes on to their\ncustomers and create bills, which in many cases, are dramatically higher\nthan public water utilities.\n\nWhen private companies seek and receive rate increases from the Public\nService Commission, the corresponding water bill spikes can be dramatic.\nConsumers required to pay these large charges deserve to know that the\ncompany's finances are in order and that all laws regulating their\ncosts, profits and expenditures are being followed.\n\nThis legislation would require the public service commission to retain\nan independent auditor to conduct audits of private water utility compa-\nnies prior to and after rate changes are approved by the public service\ncommission.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
